{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-qz-bicompletion","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:qz-bicompletion","kind":"definition","title":"$(q, z)$-bicompletion $\\widehat{\\mathbb{Z}[q^{\\pm 1}, z]}_{q,z}$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-z-habiro-ring"],"tags":["habiro-ring","bicompletion","cyclotomic-completion","brane-tower","colored-jones","open-construction"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.HabiroRing.QZBicompletionElement","text":"qz-bicompletion.md","leanSource":"qz-bicompletion.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:qz-bicompletion\"></a><p><strong>Definition.</strong>\n<em>The <strong><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(q, z)</code>-bicompletion</strong> is the inverse limit</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\widehat{\\mathbb{Z}[q^{\\pm 1}, z]}_{q,z} := \\varprojlim_{(m, n)} \\mathbb{Z}[q^{\\pm 1}, z] \\big/ \\bigl(I_{m,n}\\bigr),</code></pre>\n<p><em>indexed by pairs <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(m, n) \\in \\mathbb{N}^2</code>, with the bigraded ideal</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  I_{m,n} := \\bigl((q;q)_m \\cdot P_n(q, z)\\bigr).</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/qz-bicompletion.md","heading":"Definition","number":"13.14.7","page":"b/def-qz-bicompletion","qa":{"counts":{"pass":86,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":16,"unknown":0,"stale":76},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.HabiroRing.QZBicompletionElement","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/qz-bicompletion.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
